*> Test US12-client (spec 002; docs/protocol/40-menus-9-block-editor-screens.md section 7A, 40-menus-x1-continuation.md section 8): the test instance block editor through the real screen stack at GUI 320 x 240
*> (left 2): opened by using a test_instance_block (an INIT action is sent); the layout of 8.4 example 1; an invalid id shows Invalid test ID and greys Save; Done sends SET with the 7A.4 wire bytes; the rotation
*> cycle greys Save; the status packet 0x81 fills the info and the size boxes; Cancel sends nothing.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-SCREEN-40-9-TI.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY CCSHIM.
 COPY CONTENT.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-SERVER              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-THRESHOLD           BINARY-LONG VALUE -1.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 512.
 01 WS-HEX                 PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-X                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-Y                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 2.
 01 WS-Z                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 3.
 01 WS-STATE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ROW                 PIC X(819).
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-BODY                PIC X(8).
 01 WS-BLEN                BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-PACKET-ID           BINARY-LONG VALUE 14.
 01 WS-PACKET             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CONN               BINARY-LONG VALUE CONN-GAME.
 01 WS-STATE-A            BINARY-LONG VALUE 2.
 01 WS-KEYB                PIC X(112).
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-N                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PTR                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-D1                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-D2                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-MS                  BINARY-LONG VALUE 20.
 01 WS-E1                  PIC -(7)9.
 01 WS-E2                  PIC -(7)9.
 01 WS-E3                  PIC -(7)9.
 01 WS-E4                  PIC -(7)9.
 01 WS-EVENTS.
    05 WS-EVENT OCCURS 4 TIMES.
       10 WS-KIND          BINARY-LONG.
       10 WS-A             BINARY-LONG.
       10 WS-B             BINARY-LONG.
       10 WS-C             BINARY-LONG.
       10 WS-EX            FLOAT-SHORT.
       10 WS-EY            FLOAT-SHORT.

 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "TEST-PLAY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-SERVER
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     MOVE 640 TO IN-WIN-W
     MOVE 480 TO IN-WIN-H
     MOVE 0 TO IN-CAPTURED
     MOVE 1 TO PL-MODE
     MOVE 2 TO PL-PERM
     MOVE X"00" TO WS-BODY(1:1)
     CALL "CONTENT-CLIENT-REGISTRY-ADD" USING WS-PACKET-ID WS-BODY WS-BLEN WS-STATUS
     MOVE "test_instance_block" TO WS-KEYB
     CALL "CONTENT-BLOCK-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEYB WS-ID WS-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE WS-ROW TO CT-BLOCK-ROW
     MOVE FUNCTION NUMVAL(CT-BR-DEFAULT-STATE) TO WS-STATE
     CALL "BLOCKEDIT-USE-CHECK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-STATE
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-9§7A using a test instance block with creative and level 2 opens the form screen" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SCR-FORM TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE SM-SCREEN TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-STEP" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-HEX
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-HEX WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-x1§8 opening sends INIT (0x41, action 0, no test, size 1 1 1, rotation 0, entities kept)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "410000004000003002000001010100000000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-HEX(1:36) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-N
     PERFORM FRAME
     PERFORM BOXES
     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-x1§8 layout at W 320: id box (2, 40, 316), size boxes 2/66/131 at y 160 (56 wide), rotation 196, entities 261, Reset (2, 185, 154), Save (164, 185), Run (2, 210, 100), Done (110), Cancel (218)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "F2:40:316x20 F2:160:56x20 F66:160:56x20 F131:160:56x20 B196:160:56x20 B261:160:56x20 B2:185:154x20 B164:185:154x20 B2:210:100x20 B110:210:100x20 B218:210:100x20 " TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-x1§8 an empty id is not an identifier: the info reads Invalid test ID" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "Invalid test ID" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE EB-TI-INFO(1:EB-TI-INFO-LEN) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 50 TO WS-D1
     MOVE 50 TO WS-D2
     PERFORM CLICK-GUI
     INITIALIZE WS-EVENTS
     MOVE CC-EV-TEXT TO WS-KIND(1) WS-KIND(2) WS-KIND(3)
     MOVE 102 TO WS-A(1)
     MOVE 111 TO WS-A(2)
     MOVE 111 TO WS-A(3)
     MOVE 3 TO WS-N
     PERFORM FRAME
     MOVE 0 TO WS-N
     PERFORM FRAME
     MOVE 50 TO WS-D1
     MOVE 220 TO WS-D2
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-HEX
     CALL "TEST-STEP" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-HEX WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE 130 TO WS-D1
     MOVE 220 TO WS-D2
     PERFORM CLICK-GUI
     PERFORM FLUSH
     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-9§7A Done with id foo sends SET (action 2): test present minecraft:foo, size 1 1 1, rotation 0, ignore 0, status 0, no error" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "41000000400000300202010d6d696e6563726166743a666f6f01010100000000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-HEX(1:64) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   Rotation 90 greys Save; a status packet fills the info and sizes.
     CALL "BLOCKEDIT-USE-CHECK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-STATE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-N
     PERFORM FRAME
     MOVE 210 TO WS-D1
     MOVE 170 TO WS-D2
     PERFORM CLICK-GUI
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-x1§8 the rotation button cycles 0, 90: rotation id 1" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EB-TI-ROT TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "0" TO EF-TEXT(2)
     MOVE "99" TO EF-TEXT(3)
     MOVE 2 TO EF-LEN(3)
     MOVE "x" TO EF-TEXT(4)
     CALL "TEST-STEP" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-HEX WS-THRESHOLD
     CALL "TI-SEND" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-STATE-A
     CALL "TEST-STEP" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-HEX
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-HEX WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-x1§8 parseSize: 0 gives 1, 99 gives 48, x gives 1" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "013001" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-HEX(23:6) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     PERFORM FRAME
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 4
         MOVE 0 TO WS-N
     END-PERFORM
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE 129 TO WS-PACKET
     MOVE PB-TEXT-PLAIN TO PB-TX-KIND
     MOVE 13 TO PB-TX-LENGTH
     MOVE "Function: foo" TO PB-TX-VALUE
     MOVE 0 TO PB-TX-ARG-COUNT
     CALL "PB-PUT-TEXT" USING PB-BUFFER PB-TEXT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-I
     CALL "PB-PUT-BOOL" USING PB-BUFFER WS-I
     MOVE 3 TO WS-I
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-I
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-I
     MOVE 7 TO WS-I
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-I
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     CALL "PROTO-PACKET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN PB-BUFFER WS-PACKET
     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-x1§8 the status packet 0x81 sets the info (Function: foo) and the size boxes (3, 3, 7)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "Function: foo|3|3|7" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING EB-TI-INFO(1:EB-TI-INFO-LEN) "|" EF-TEXT(2)(1:EF-LEN(2)) "|" EF-TEXT(3)(1:EF-LEN(3)) "|" EF-TEXT(4)(1:EF-LEN(4)) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   Entities, Reset, Save (rotation 0 and a valid id), Run, Cancel; a status with the screen closed changes nothing.
     MOVE 270 TO WS-D1
     MOVE 170 TO WS-D2
     PERFORM CLICK-GUI
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-x1§8 the include entities button toggles the flag (on to off)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EB-TI-ENT TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 50 TO WS-D1
     MOVE 50 TO WS-D2
     PERFORM CLICK-GUI
     INITIALIZE WS-EVENTS
     MOVE CC-EV-TEXT TO WS-KIND(1) WS-KIND(2)
     MOVE 97 TO WS-A(1)
     MOVE 98 TO WS-A(2)
     MOVE 2 TO WS-N
     PERFORM FRAME
     MOVE 0 TO EB-TI-ROT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-N
     PERFORM FRAME
     MOVE 100 TO WS-D1
     MOVE 195 TO WS-D2
     PERFORM CLICK-GUI
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-x1§8 Reset (2, 185) sends RESET and closes" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SCR-WORLD TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE SM-SCREEN TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "BLOCKEDIT-USE-CHECK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-STATE
     MOVE "ab" TO EF-TEXT(1)
     MOVE 2 TO EF-LEN(1)
     MOVE 0 TO WS-N
     PERFORM FRAME
     MOVE 200 TO WS-D1
     MOVE 195 TO WS-D2
     PERFORM CLICK-GUI
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-x1§8 Save (164, 185) with rotation NONE and a valid id sends SAVE and closes" TO TL-CASE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "BLOCKEDIT-USE-CHECK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-STATE
     MOVE 1 TO EB-TI-ROT
     MOVE "ab" TO EF-TEXT(1)
     MOVE 2 TO EF-LEN(1)
     MOVE 0 TO WS-N
     PERFORM FRAME
     MOVE 200 TO WS-D1
     MOVE 195 TO WS-D2
     PERFORM CLICK-GUI
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-x1§8 Save with rotation 90 does nothing: the screen stays" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SCR-FORM TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE SM-SCREEN TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 50 TO WS-D1
     MOVE 220 TO WS-D2
     PERFORM CLICK-GUI
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-x1§8 Run (2, 210) sends RUN and closes" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SCR-WORLD TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE SM-SCREEN TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "BLOCKEDIT-USE-CHECK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-STATE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-N
     PERFORM FRAME
     MOVE 250 TO WS-D1
     MOVE 220 TO WS-D2
     PERFORM CLICK-GUI
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-x1§8 Cancel (218, 210) closes with no further action" TO TL-CASE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "CONTENT-CLOSE"
     STOP RUN.

 FRAME.
     CALL "TEST-EVENTS-MS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EVENTS WS-N WS-MS
     CALL "SCREEN-BUILD" USING CLIENT-STATE
     INITIALIZE WS-EVENTS
     .

 FLUSH.
     CALL "TEST-STEP" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-HEX
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-HEX WS-THRESHOLD
     .

 CLICK-GUI.
     INITIALIZE WS-EVENTS
     MOVE CC-EV-CURSOR TO WS-KIND(1)
     COMPUTE WS-EX(1) = WS-D1 * 2
     COMPUTE WS-EY(1) = WS-D2 * 2
     MOVE WS-EX(1) TO WS-EX(2) WS-EX(3)
     MOVE WS-EY(1) TO WS-EY(2) WS-EY(3)
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-DOWN TO WS-KIND(2)
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-UP TO WS-KIND(3)
     MOVE 3 TO WS-N
     CALL "TEST-EVENTS-MS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EVENTS WS-N WS-MS
     CALL "SCREEN-BUILD" USING CLIENT-STATE
     INITIALIZE WS-EVENTS
     .

*> TL-OBSERVED: the field overlays (F) and the buttons (B) as "Fx:y:wxh " in widget order.
 BOXES.
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PTR
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 2 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > SM-WIDGET-COUNT
         IF (SM-W-KIND(WS-I) = WK-OVERLAY AND SM-W-ARG(WS-I) = SW-FIELD) OR SM-W-KIND(WS-I) = WK-BUTTON
             MOVE SM-W-X(WS-I) TO WS-E1
             MOVE SM-W-Y(WS-I) TO WS-E2
             MOVE SM-W-W(WS-I) TO WS-E3
             MOVE SM-W-H(WS-I) TO WS-E4
             IF SM-W-KIND(WS-I) = WK-BUTTON
                 STRING "B" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) ":" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) ":" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E3) "x" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E4) " " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
             ELSE
                 STRING "F" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) ":" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) ":" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E3) "x" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E4) " " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
             END-IF
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     .

 END PROGRAM TEST-SCREEN-40-9-TI.

 COPY CLTEST.
